system "ISO:ara-Arab:Latn:233-2026" {

metadata {
  authority_id iso
  id 233-2026
  language iso-639-2:ara
  source_script Arab
  destination_script Latn
  name "ISO 233-1:2026 Information and documentation -- Transliteration of Perso-Arabic characters into Latin characters -- Part 1: Arabic language (strict transliteration, clause 4; FDIS stage)"
  url https://www.iso.org/committee/48820.html
  creation_date 2026
  adoption_date 2026
  description {    Strict (fully reversible, level (a)) transliteration of ISO 233-1:2026, clause 4,
    Tables 1-5: written signs only, diacritical vowels transliterated only where written
    in the source. Encoded from the committee ballot ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N129 (FDIS,
    2026-11-02; ballot closed 2026-11-07) with the comment adjudications of N130.
    See notes for provenance, errata and reversibility.  }

  notes {
    note "Encoded from ISO/FDIS 233-1:2026, ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N129 (2026-11-02, FDIS ballot closed 2026-11-07), clause 4 Tables 1-5; adjudications honored from the collated comments N130: DE-002 accepted (hamzaẗ al-waṣl renders 02BE+0331), CN-017 rejected (alif treatment intentionally differs between strict and modified), CN-016 rejected (Table 4 intentionally lists only Arabic-encoded punctuation). Source documents archived in interscript/interscript-private-references (iso/ISO-TC46-WG3-N129-*, N130-*). Verify against the published edition when available. The FDIS cancels and replaces ISO 233:1984 and ISO 233-2:1993: new work uses this map while the legacy corpus maps iso-ara-Arab-Latn-233-1984 and iso-ara-Arab-Latn-233-2-1993 remain for existing data. ISO 233-3:2026 (Persian) is a separate part, already published; its legacy corpus coverage is iso-prs-Arab-Latn-233-3-1999."
    note "Three levels of transliteration (Introduction): this map implements level (a), strict fully reversible, written signs only. Level (b) - strict with the diacritical vowels supplied regardless of the source - is an application mode of the same Tables 1-2, not a separate table; a stateless map cannot supply unwritten vowels, so the level is documented here rather than forced into the map."
    note "Reversibility (4.1.3) holds one-to-one for every row except the merger the standard itself prescribes: Table 1 No. 2a maps both U+0654 and U+0655 to 02C8, so the reverse direction restores 0654. The foreword legacy variants for existing text (02BC, 0329, 02B9, 02BB) are notes, not rules of this map."
    note "4.1.4 precomposed/decomposed equality: the map adds canonical-decomposition equivalents of the precomposed alef forms (0623, 0625, 0624, 0626; 0622 is a table row itself) and decomposes the šadda-haraka ligatures U+FC5F..U+FC63 in the normalization pass. Letter positional presentation forms (U+FE70..U+FEFF; Annex A is informative) pass through unchanged."
    note "Mark order: a first pass normalizes harakat+šadda to šadda+harakat (NFC orders harakat ccc 30-32 before šadda ccc 33; the FDIS examples decompose U+FC60 shadda-first), so every source order transliterates identically and the šadda macron (0304) attaches to the consonant output. Per Table 3 footnote a, the macron above ā, ī, ū does not represent šaddaẗ - the precomposed ā/ī/ū outputs of the vowel rows are vowels, not šadda."
    note "4.3.2 examples: example 1 (أَلشَّمْسُ ʾˈalš̄am̊su) is conformant with the tables and is tested verbatim in NFC-composed form. Printed examples 2-3 are errata: bi-̓llaẙli carries the DIS rendering of U+0671 (U+002D+U+0313) that DE-002 replaced with 02BE+0331 and omits the šadda macron; lilwaladi omits the sukūn ring. The rule-derived forms are tested instead (N130 CN-019: 4.3.2 and 5.3.2 intentionally represent different methods)."
  }
}

dependency "ara-latn-233-2026" as iso233

tests {
  # Hand-written worked-example and structure tests.
  "\u0623\u064e\u0644\u0634\u0651\u064e\u0645\u0652\u0633\u064f" -> "\u02be\u02c8al\u0161\u0304am\u030asu"  # 4.3.2 example 1 verbatim: ʾˈalš̄am̊su
  "\u0646\u064e\u0642\u0650\u0641\u064f" -> "naqifu"  # Introduction worked example: naqifu
  "\u0646\u0642\u0641" -> "nqf"  # Introduction worked example: nqf (unvocalized)
  "\u0623\u064e\u062e" -> "\u02be\u02c8a\u1e96"  # 4.1.4 precomposed أَ -> ʾˈa
  "\u0627\u0654\u064e\u062e" -> "\u02be\u02c8a\u1e96"  # 4.1.4 decomposed ا+0654+َ identical
  "\u0634\ufc60\u0645" -> "\u0161\u0304am"  # U+FC60 ligature
  "\u0634\u064e\u0651\u0645" -> "\u0161\u0304am"  # NFC order identical
  "\u0634\u0651\u064e\u0645" -> "\u0161\u0304am"  # typed order identical
  "\u0628\u0651" -> "b\u0304"  # šadda macron attaches to the consonant
  "\u0645\u0652" -> "m\u030a"  # sukūn ring attaches to the consonant
  "\u0628\u0651\u064e\u0642\u064f" -> "b\u0304aqu"  # šadda macron stays on the consonant before a following vowel

  # Hand-written worked-example and structure tests below; the exhaustive per-row tests
  # follow, generated from the source document's tables (Tables 1-5, 57 rows: 56 document rows, No. 2a split into its 0654/0655 pair).
  # Source: ISO/FDIS 233-1:2026, ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N129 (FDIS for ballot, 2026-11-02;
  # ballot closed 2026-11-07), clause 4. Adjudications: ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N130 collated
  # comments. Expected strings are the map outputs (precomposed Latin per the hex
  # columns; combining marks 030A/0304/0331 attach to the preceding output character).
  # Provenance artifact: scripts/row-sources/iso-ara-Arab-Latn-233-2026.json (57 rows).
  # generated-by: maps/scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs (2026-11-19); regenerate from the artifact, do not hand-edit.
# Exhaustive per-row tests for iso-ara-Arab-Latn-233-2026, generated from the source
# document's table.
# Source: ISO 233-1:2026 (FDIS) strict transliteration, clause 4 Tables 1-5,
# 57 rows (56 document rows; the 0654-or-0655 pair of No. 2a split) in
# document order: Table 1 consonants (No. 1-29a including 1a/2a; the
# 0654-or-0655 pair of No. 2a encoded as two rows sharing 02C8 per the
# standard), Table 2 vowels for the fully reversible system (No. 30-32a; the
# foreword's á-to-ã, í-to-ĩ, ú-to-ũ changes), Table 3 other conventional
# signs (No. 33 sukūn 030A, No. 34 šadda 0304 with footnote a 'The macron
# above ā, ī, ū does not represent šaddaẗ', No. 35 hamzat al-waṣl 02BE+0331
# per the accepted DE-002), Table 4 punctuation (the CN-016 rejection:
# intentionally only Arabic-encoded marks), Table 5 numerals. Source: ISO/TC
# 46/WG 3 N129 (ISO_FDIS 233-1 ed.1, 2026-11-02; ballot closed 2026-11-07),
# hex columns authoritative, cross-checked against the N130 collated
# comments. Ballot documents archived in
# interscript/interscript-private-references (iso/ISO-TC46-WG3-N129-* and
# N130-*). Verify against the published edition when available.
# Provenance artifact: scripts/row-sources/iso-ara-Arab-Latn-233-2026.json (57 rows).
# generated-by: maps/scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs (2026-11-19); regenerate from the artifact, do not hand-edit.
  "ا" -> "ʾ"
  "آ" -> "ʾâ"
  "ء" -> "ˌ"
  "ٔ" -> "ˈ"
  "ٕ" -> "ˈ"
  "ب" -> "b"
  "ت" -> "t"
  "ث" -> "ṯ"
  "ج" -> "ǧ"
  "ح" -> "ḥ"
  "خ" -> "ẖ"
  "د" -> "d"
  "ذ" -> "ḏ"
  "ر" -> "r"
  "ز" -> "z"
  "س" -> "s"
  "ش" -> "š"
  "ص" -> "ṣ"
  "ض" -> "ḍ"
  "ط" -> "ṭ"
  "ظ" -> "ẓ"
  "ع" -> "ʿ"
  "غ" -> "ġ"
  "ف" -> "f"
  "ق" -> "q"
  "ك" -> "k"
  "ل" -> "l"
  "م" -> "m"
  "ن" -> "n"
  "ه" -> "h"
  "ة" -> "ẗ"
  "و" -> "w"
  "ي" -> "y"
  "ى" -> "ỳ"
  "َ" -> "a"
  "ٰ" -> "ā"
  "ً" -> "ã"
  "ُ" -> "u"
  "ٌ" -> "ũ"
  "ِ" -> "i"
  "ٍ" -> "ĩ"
  "ْ" -> "̊"
  "ّ" -> "̄"
  "ٱ" -> "ʾ̱"
  "،" -> ","
  "؛" -> ";"
  "؟" -> "?"
  "٠" -> "0"
  "١" -> "1"
  "٢" -> "2"
  "٣" -> "3"
  "٤" -> "4"
  "٥" -> "5"
  "٦" -> "6"
  "٧" -> "7"
  "٨" -> "8"
  "٩" -> "9"
}

stage main {
  # Pass 1: mark-order and ligature normalization. NFC canonical order places
  # harakat (ccc 30-32) before šadda (ccc 33); the FDIS examples decompose
  # U+FC60 shadda-first. This pass normalizes harakat+šadda to šadda+harakat
  # and decomposes the šadda ligatures, so every source order transliterates
  # identically and the šadda output attaches to the consonant (Table 3
  # footnote a: the macron above ā, ī, ū does not represent šaddaẗ).
  parallel {
    sub "\ufc5f" "\u0651\u064d"
    sub "\ufc60" "\u0651\u064e"
    sub "\ufc61" "\u0651\u064f"
    sub "\ufc62" "\u0651\u0650"
    sub "\ufc63" "\u0651\u0670"
    sub "\u064e\u0651" "\u0651\u064e"
    sub "\u064f\u0651" "\u0651\u064f"
    sub "\u0650\u0651" "\u0651\u0650"
    sub "\u064b\u0651" "\u0651\u064b"
    sub "\u064c\u0651" "\u0651\u064c"
    sub "\u064d\u0651" "\u0651\u064d"
  }

  # Pass 2: Tables 1-5 (clause 4). Single-constraint-free parallel pass (trie semantics).
  parallel {
    use iso233.consonants
    use iso233.short_vowels
    use iso233.punctuation
    use iso233.numerals
    # Table 1 No. 1: alif
    sub "\u0627" "\u02be"
    # Table 1 No. 1a: alif maddaẗ
    sub "\u0622" "\u02be\u00e2"
    # Table 1 No. 2: hamzaẗ (footnote b: legacy combining vertical line below 0329)
    sub "\u0621" "\u02cc"
    # Table 1 No. 2a: hamzaẗ combining above/below (footnote c: legacy modifier letter prime 02B9)
    sub "\u0654" "\u02c8"
    sub "\u0655" "\u02c8"
    # Table 1 No. 29a: alif maqṣūraẗ
    sub "\u0649" "\u1ef3"
    # 4.1.4: canonical-decomposition equivalents of the precomposed alef forms
    sub "\u0623" "\u02be\u02c8"
    sub "\u0625" "\u02be\u02c8"
    sub "\u0624" "w\u02c8"
    sub "\u0626" "y\u02c8"
    # Table 2 No. 30a: alif ẖanǧariyyaẗ
    sub "\u0670" "\u0101"
    # Table 2 No. 30b/31a/32a: tanwīn (foreword: á→ã, í→ĩ, ú→ũ)
    sub "\u064b" "\u00e3"
    sub "\u064c" "\u0169"
    sub "\u064d" "\u0129"
    # Table 3 No. 33: sukūn (combining ring above)
    sub "\u0652" "\u030a"
    # Table 3 No. 34: šaddaẗ (combining macron; footnote a)
    sub "\u0651" "\u0304"
    # Table 3 No. 35: hamzaẗ al-waṣl 02BE+0331 (N130 DE-002 accepted)
    sub "\u0671" "\u02be\u0331"
  }
}
}
